971
00:42:59.050 --> 00:43:02.290
in Louisville, Kentucky, and many others, by the way,
她来自肯塔基州路易斯维尔，顺便说一下，还有很多人也指出来了，

972
00:43:02.490 --> 00:43:05.590
who said, I think there's a math error.
她说，我觉得这里有个数学错误。

973
00:43:06.510 --> 00:43:08.190
Helene says she's 49.
海琳说她49岁。

974
00:43:08.750 --> 00:43:10.990
Pam says it's the ninth year in a row.
帕姆说是连续第九年了。

975
00:43:10.990 --> 00:43:19.570
But if she first celebrated her 49th birthday on her 49th birthday, that counts as one of the nine.
但如果她第一次庆祝49岁生日是在她49岁那年，那就算作九年里的第一年。

976
00:43:19.790 --> 00:43:27.150
So you would actually add 49 plus eight additional birthdays, which means Helene is really turning 57.
所以你实际上应该用49加上额外的八个生日，这意味着海琳其实是要过57岁生日。

977
00:43:28.070 --> 00:43:29.190
Nice catch.
发现得好。

978
00:43:29.610 --> 00:43:30.030
Yeah.
是啊。

979
00:43:30.410 --> 00:43:38.310
So when I was trading messages with Charlie Grandy about this episode, he said that what he remembers most about working with Seth Gordon
所以当我和查理·格兰迪交流这一集时，他说他关于和塞斯·戈登合作最深刻的记忆是，

980
00:43:38.310 --> 00:43:47.590
was the fact that me, John, Steve, and Linda were going to be locked at this same table for, like, four big scenes in a row.
我和约翰、史蒂夫还有琳达要被锁在同一张桌子旁，连续拍四场大戏。

981
00:43:47.950 --> 00:43:53.610
And it became this big question, how are we going to visually differentiate these scenes?
于是这就成了一个大问题，我们要怎么在视觉上区分这些场景呢？

982
00:43:53.730 --> 00:43:56.470
How are we going to make them feel alive?
我们要怎么让它们看起来生动呢？

983
00:43:56.470 --> 00:43:56.990
Right.
对。

984
00:43:57.710 --> 00:44:02.850
And Charlie said, if you rewatch it, you can really see what a great job he did.
查理说，如果你重看一遍，真的能看出他做得有多棒。

985
00:44:03.030 --> 00:44:04.870
He added multiple angles.
他增加了多个角度。

986
00:44:04.990 --> 00:44:07.610
He keeps flipping sides to keep it interesting.
他不断切换拍摄侧面来保持新鲜感。

987
00:44:07.910 --> 00:44:15.690
And by mostly framing out the other tables, he does a great job of shrinking what was a really big space
而且通过尽量避开其他桌子的构图，他成功地缩小了原本很大的空间，

988
00:44:15.690 --> 00:44:20.650
and, quote, imprisoning you in Michael's awkwardness.
并且，引用他的话，把你“囚禁”在迈克尔的尴尬之中。

989
00:44:21.130 --> 00:44:22.910
Ooh, that's so artsy.
噢，那太有艺术感了。

990
00:44:23.070 --> 00:44:23.690
I know.
我知道。

991
00:44:23.690 --> 00:44:25.070
And it's really true.
而且确实如此。

992
00:44:25.070 --> 00:44:35.730
I started rewatching these scenes, and we only used two cameras, but in each of the scenes, they set them up a little differently.
我开始重看这些场景，我们只用了两台摄像机，但在每一场戏里，他们设置的角度都略有不同。

993
00:44:35.730 --> 00:44:38.930
So you didn't feel like you were coming back to the same table.
所以你不会觉得你是在回到同一张桌子。

994
00:44:39.050 --> 00:44:44.730
And as the scenes go on, the camera gets closer and closer and closer.
随着场景推进，镜头越来越近，越来越近。

995
00:44:44.730 --> 00:44:49.470
So you really are, like, going into Michael's, like, little mind.
所以你真的就像是，走进了迈克尔那小小的内心世界。

996
00:44:49.790 --> 00:44:50.690
It's cool.
很酷。

997
00:44:50.890 --> 00:44:51.790
It's really cool.
真的很酷。

998
00:44:52.070 --> 00:45:00.930
Well, we're going to go from this talk of being 49 nine years in a row, but actually being 58 with more sexy talk.
好了，我们要从这关于连续九年49岁，但实际上是58岁的话题，转到更多性感的话题了。

999
00:45:01.430 --> 00:45:03.750
What name should she be called, Nana or Grandma?
她该叫什么名字，娜娜还是奶奶？

1000
00:45:04.310 --> 00:45:04.710
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1001
00:45:04.850 --> 00:45:06.590
Michael's really feeling it now.
迈克尔现在真的很有感觉。

1002
00:45:06.850 --> 00:45:07.670
He is.
确实。

1003
00:45:07.670 --> 00:45:11.670
I noticed something at nine minutes and six seconds in this scene.
我注意到这一幕在九分零六秒时有个细节。

1004
00:45:12.010 --> 00:45:12.170
What?
什么？

1005
00:45:12.570 --> 00:45:16.550
Do you notice how Steve eats his food as Michael Scott?
你注意到史蒂夫在演迈克尔·斯科特时是怎么吃东西的吗？

1006
00:45:17.190 --> 00:45:20.110
It's exactly how he ate in Dinner Party.
和他演《晚宴》时吃东西的方式一模一样。

1007
00:45:20.550 --> 00:45:23.390
Well, he kind of scrapes the fork with his teeth.
嗯，他吃的时候会用牙齿刮叉子。

1008
00:45:23.750 --> 00:45:24.210
Yes.
没错。

1009
00:45:24.470 --> 00:45:31.070
He eats tiny amounts of food off the tip of the fork with his very front teeth.
他用最前面的牙齿从叉尖上一点点地吃东西。

1010
00:45:31.070 --> 00:45:34.010
He doesn't put the fork all the way in his mouth.
他不会把叉子整个放进嘴里。

1011
00:45:34.430 --> 00:45:37.230
He, like, bites it off the tip of the fork.
他就像是把食物从叉尖上咬下来一样。

1012
00:45:37.730 --> 00:45:38.710
It's very interesting.
这很有意思。

1013
00:45:38.790 --> 00:45:40.530
He does not eat this way in real life.
他在现实生活中不是这样吃东西的。

1014
00:45:40.530 --> 00:45:42.370
I've dined with him many times.
我和他一起吃过很多次饭。

1015
00:45:42.750 --> 00:45:46.070
This is clearly a Michael Scott eating choice.
这显然是迈克尔·斯科特式的进食选择。

1016
00:45:46.310 --> 00:45:53.370
It's either a Michael Scott eating choice or it's Steve the actor not wanting to eat the prop food and making the best of it.
这要么是迈克尔·斯科特的进食选择，要么是演员史蒂夫不想吃道具食物，所以尽量少吃点。

1017
00:45:53.390 --> 00:45:55.170
Because I would do something similar.
因为我也会做类似的事。

1018
00:45:55.170 --> 00:46:01.510
I would just put the tiniest amount, like, on the end of the fork or spoon so I didn't have to eat too much of it.
我只会放极少的一点点在叉子或勺子尖上，这样我就不用吃太多了。

1019
00:46:01.750 --> 00:46:14.030
Well, now I guess I'd have to watch Steve's other films and see if he's eating in any of them and see if this is just his actor way of eating or if it was a character choice.
好吧，我想我得去看看史蒂夫的其他电影，看看他在里面是怎么吃的，确认这到底是他的表演习惯，还是角色设定。

1020
00:46:14.170 --> 00:46:14.730
I'll investigate.
我会去调查一下。

1021
00:46:15.330 --> 00:46:15.770
Investigate.
调查一下吧。

1022
00:46:15.830 --> 00:46:21.650
Because with prop food, when you start out, it's usually really fresh and warm and they've made it ready for you to eat.
因为道具食物刚开始的时候通常很新鲜、很热，是专门为你准备的。

1023
00:46:21.650 --> 00:46:28.810
But as each take goes, it gets colder and colder and a little bit more wilty, depending what you're eating.
但随着拍摄次数增加，食物会越来越凉，根据食物种类不同，还会变得有点蔫。

1024
00:46:29.050 --> 00:46:32.630
And I just found early on the smaller bites are better.
我早早就发现，吃小口一点比较好。

1025
00:46:33.050 --> 00:46:33.230
True.
确实。

1026
00:46:33.870 --> 00:46:36.390
It's also lunchtime back at Dunder Mifflin.
邓德·米夫林那边也到了午餐时间。

1027
00:46:36.710 --> 00:46:41.890
And, oh my gosh, Andy has set up a whole taco buffet in the conference room.
天哪，安迪在会议室里摆了一整桌塔可自助餐。

1028
00:46:42.330 --> 00:46:45.390
Yes, but Dwight is going to volunteer to serve everyone.
是的，但德怀特主动提出要为大家服务。

1029
00:46:45.570 --> 00:46:45.890
Yes.
没错。

1030
00:46:46.190 --> 00:46:50.290
Did you notice at 9 minutes 26 seconds when Angela Martin enters?
你注意到九分二十六秒安吉拉·马丁进来的时候了吗？

1031
00:46:50.890 --> 00:46:51.390
Yes.
注意到了。

1032
00:46:51.670 --> 00:46:54.350
Her face she makes and she does a 180 out of the room?
她做的那个表情，然后直接转身走出了房间？

1033
00:46:54.610 --> 00:46:55.830
Well, because she's vegetarian.
嗯，因为她是素食主义者。

1034
00:46:56.210 --> 00:47:00.550
So I went to the script because I was like, what did it say in the script about this moment?
所以我去查了剧本，因为我在想，剧本里是怎么写这一刻的？

1035
00:47:00.830 --> 00:47:05.150
In the script, it just says Angela Martin enters the room and immediately walks back out.
剧本里只写了安吉拉·马丁走进房间，然后立刻又走了出去。

1036
00:47:05.810 --> 00:47:06.310
Oh.
哦。

1037
00:47:06.570 --> 00:47:11.650
So the face I made was just me, like probably playing around in the moment.
所以我做的那个表情纯粹是我自己当时在现场即兴发挥的。

1038
00:47:11.930 --> 00:47:13.070
I have a question.
我有个问题。

1039
00:47:13.410 --> 00:47:15.850
Did you guys actually eat those tacos that day?
你们那天真的吃了那些塔可吗？

1040
00:47:15.850 --> 00:47:16.770
They looked good.
看起来很好吃。

1041
00:47:17.550 --> 00:47:20.330
We did not just because it had to sit there for a bit.
我们没吃，因为它们得在那儿放上一会儿。

1042
00:47:20.490 --> 00:47:20.850
Oh.
哦。

1043
00:47:21.010 --> 00:47:23.730
But we wanted to, when they first brought them out, we're like, woo-hoo, tacos.
但刚端出来的时候我们确实想吃，当时我们都在欢呼：呜呼，塔可！

1044
00:47:23.930 --> 00:47:24.970
And we're like, no, no, no, guys.
然后我们又说：不不不，伙计们，别吃。

1045
00:47:25.450 --> 00:47:30.030
There's also a Kevin talking head and little moment that got deleted, probably for time.
还有一个凯文的采访片段和一小段戏被删掉了，可能是因为时长原因。

1046
00:47:30.190 --> 00:47:30.950
I loved it.
我很喜欢那段。

1047
00:47:31.470 --> 00:47:34.670
Kevin is so excited that Dwight is going to serve the tacos.
凯文对德怀特要来分发塔可感到非常兴奋。

1048
00:47:35.330 --> 00:47:36.850
And he has this talking head.
他还有一段采访。

1049
00:47:37.390 --> 00:47:38.350
This is great.
这太棒了。

1050
00:47:38.350 --> 00:47:39.350
I love tacos.
我爱吃塔可。

1051
00:47:39.590 --> 00:47:43.030
But whenever I try to make one, I get too excited and I crush it.
但每当我试着做一个的时候，我都会太激动，然后把它捏碎了。

1052
00:47:43.270 --> 00:47:43.750
Oh.
噢。

1053
00:47:44.230 --> 00:47:48.110
And so then it cuts back to the scene and Dwight's making his taco.
然后镜头切回那个场景，德怀特正在做他的塔可饼。

1054
00:47:48.550 --> 00:47:49.750
Dwight hands it to Kevin.
德怀特把它递给凯文。

1055
00:47:49.970 --> 00:47:52.030
And Kevin's so excited, he crushes it in his hand.
凯文太激动了，他一把把它捏碎了。

1056
00:47:52.170 --> 00:47:54.010
Oh, Kevin.
噢，凯文。

1057
00:47:55.650 --> 00:47:59.110
Well, after these guys compete to see who's going to serve the tacos,
好吧，在这些人比赛看谁来供应塔可饼之后，

1058
00:47:59.270 --> 00:48:01.810
now they're going to compete to see who's going to clean them up.
现在他们又要比赛看谁来清理残局了。

1059
00:48:02.050 --> 00:48:03.050
It doesn't stop.
没完没了。

1060
00:48:03.150 --> 00:48:04.030
It doesn't stop.
没完没了。

1061
00:48:04.660 --> 00:48:07.710
Jenna, I'd like to break down all the gifts that Michael got Helene.
珍娜，我想盘点一下迈克尔送给海琳的所有礼物。

1062
00:48:08.250 --> 00:48:08.710
Oh.
噢。

1063
00:48:08.990 --> 00:48:11.350
And really show how all out he went for her.
并展示他为了她有多么倾其所有。

1064
00:48:11.530 --> 00:48:13.010
Until he broke up with her.
直到他跟她分手。

1065
00:48:13.950 --> 00:48:15.130
He went all out.
他确实倾其所有了。

1066
00:48:15.430 --> 00:48:19.590
He got her the necklace and then also the lunch reservation, right?
他送了她项链，还有午餐预订，对吧？

1067
00:48:19.770 --> 00:48:20.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1068
00:48:20.310 --> 00:48:22.030
Where he decorated the table.
他在那里装饰了餐桌。

1069
00:48:22.250 --> 00:48:24.430
I counted eight balloons, a birthday banner,
我数了数，有八个气球，一个生日横幅，

1070
00:48:24.510 --> 00:48:29.130
and also a really beautiful flower arrangement that none of the other tables had.
还有一束非常漂亮的花，其他桌子都没有。

1071
00:48:29.270 --> 00:48:29.550
Yes.
是的。

1072
00:48:29.710 --> 00:48:31.470
I assume she can take that with her.
我想她可以把那些带走。

1073
00:48:31.650 --> 00:48:32.110
Yes.
是的。

1074
00:48:32.110 --> 00:48:37.250
As well as a scrapbook of their courtship, the wrapping paper says love in several different
还有一本记录他们恋爱过程的剪贴簿，包装纸上用好几种语言写着爱，

1075
00:48:37.250 --> 00:48:37.690
languages.
语言。

1076
00:48:38.370 --> 00:48:41.310
Here are a few things that were in the scrapbook per the shooting draft.
根据拍摄剧本，剪贴簿里有以下几样东西。

1077
00:48:41.490 --> 00:48:42.630
Some made it in the episode.
有些出现在了剧集中。

1078
00:48:42.810 --> 00:48:43.450
Some did not.
有些没有。

1079
00:48:43.850 --> 00:48:44.090
Oh.
噢。

1080
00:48:44.090 --> 00:48:47.730
The penny that Helene threw into the wishing well at the mall.
海琳扔进商场许愿池里的那枚硬币。

1081
00:48:47.990 --> 00:48:49.330
Which doesn't exiSt.
那个许愿池根本不存在。

1082
00:48:49.830 --> 00:48:50.450
Right.
没错。

1083
00:48:51.010 --> 00:48:53.010
The fountain that doesn't exiSt.
那个不存在的喷泉。

1084
00:48:53.790 --> 00:48:58.770
Also, a ticket stub to a movie they went to together, Love Happens.
还有一张他们一起去看的电影《爱上你》的票根。

1085
00:48:58.770 --> 00:48:59.550
Oh.
噢。

1086
00:48:59.790 --> 00:49:01.050
I looked up Love Happens.
我查了一下《爱上你》这部电影。

1087
00:49:01.130 --> 00:49:05.210
It was a movie that was out in 2009 starring Jennifer Aniston and Aaron Eckhart.
那是2009年上映的一部电影，由詹妮弗·安妮斯顿和艾伦·艾克哈特主演。

1088
00:49:05.830 --> 00:49:10.730
As well as the poem that Michael wrote slash plagiarized from Shel Silverstein.
还有迈克尔写给她的诗，或者说是抄袭自谢尔·希尔弗斯坦的诗。

1089
00:49:11.390 --> 00:49:11.810
Hmm.
嗯。

1090
00:49:12.110 --> 00:49:13.090
Here was the poem.
诗的内容是这样的。

1091
00:49:13.370 --> 00:49:16.790
I cannot go to school today, said little Peggy Ann McKay.
我今天不能去上学，小佩吉·安·麦凯说。

1092
00:49:16.950 --> 00:49:20.430
I have the measles and the mumps, a gash, a rash, and purple bumps.
我得了麻疹和腮腺炎，还有伤口、皮疹和紫色肿块。

1093
00:49:20.650 --> 00:49:22.170
My teacher's really mean.
我的老师真的很刻薄。

1094
00:49:22.410 --> 00:49:23.030
Happy birthday.
生日快乐。

1095
00:49:23.030 --> 00:49:24.250
I love you, Helene.
我爱你，海琳。

1096
00:49:24.870 --> 00:49:26.850
I mean, it's beautiful.
我是说，这太美了。

1097
00:49:27.090 --> 00:49:28.350
It might be in my journal.
它可能在我的日记里。

1098
00:49:30.490 --> 00:49:34.610
We had a fan question about the scrapbook from Carla B.
我们收到一个关于剪贴簿的粉丝提问，来自加利福尼亚州加迪纳的卡拉·B。

1099
00:49:34.830 --> 00:49:36.210
in Gardena, California.
加利福尼亚州加迪纳。

1100
00:49:37.030 --> 00:49:43.610
The cover page of the scrapbook at the very bottom where it says Love Copyright Michael.
剪贴簿的封面最底部写着爱，版权所有：迈克尔。

1101
00:49:44.090 --> 00:49:47.390
We also see the letters XXLR.
我们还看到了XXLR这几个字母。

1102
00:49:47.990 --> 00:49:50.110
Any idea what those letters stand for?
知道这几个字母代表什么吗？

1103
00:49:50.970 --> 00:49:52.390
Do you know, Ange?
你知道吗，安吉？

1104
00:49:52.430 --> 00:49:52.810
I do.
我知道。

1105
00:49:53.030 --> 00:49:53.630
What is it?
是什么？

1106
00:49:53.670 --> 00:49:54.750
It's in the shooting draft.
剧本定稿里有写。

1107
00:49:55.030 --> 00:49:55.730
Oh, tell us.
噢，告诉我们吧。

1108
00:49:55.770 --> 00:50:00.510
Because I thought they were Roman numerals, but when I looked it up, there's no R in Roman
因为我原以为那是罗马数字，但我查了一下，罗马数字里根本没有R。

1109
00:50:00.510 --> 00:50:01.090
numerals.
数字。

1110
00:50:01.210 --> 00:50:01.490
Yes.
没错。

1111
00:50:01.670 --> 00:50:05.890
So Helene reads that out loud, kind of like curious, and Michael goes, those are Roman
海琳把它读了出来，听起来有点好奇，然后迈克尔说，那是罗马

1112
00:50:05.890 --> 00:50:06.270
numerals.
数字。

1113
00:50:06.330 --> 00:50:07.010
I made them up.
是我编的。

1114
00:50:07.330 --> 00:50:08.630
Oh, my gosh!
天哪！

1115
00:50:09.390 --> 00:50:12.750
I did not know that you knew the answer to that question when I asked it.
我问那个问题的时候，真不知道你竟然知道答案。

1116
00:50:13.170 --> 00:50:14.550
Yeah, it's in the shooting draft.
是啊，剧本定稿里有写。

1117
00:50:15.290 --> 00:50:16.870
Oh, the shooting draft.
