00:56:53.740 --> 00:56:54.500
and kills a pig.
然后杀一头猪。

1283
00:56:54.660 --> 00:56:55.520
That's his workout.
那是他的锻炼方式。

1284
00:56:55.760 --> 00:56:56.780
He's not like us.
他跟我们不一样。

1285
00:56:56.880 --> 00:56:58.180
But today he tried.
但今天他努力了。

1286
00:56:58.180 --> 00:57:01.140
And you know, it wasn't too long ago, I had a temper.
你们知道，不久前，我脾气还很暴躁。

1287
00:57:01.760 --> 00:57:03.280
I was a real bastard.
我那时真是个混蛋。

1288
00:57:03.540 --> 00:57:05.100
And do you know what got me out of it?
你们知道是什么让我走出来的吗？

1289
00:57:05.580 --> 00:57:10.480
Oscar comes in with some snark and says, mandatory anger management.
奥斯卡插嘴讽刺道，强制性的愤怒管理课程。

1290
00:57:11.600 --> 00:57:13.940
We're calling back all this stuff.
我们正在回顾所有这些往事。

1291
00:57:14.180 --> 00:57:14.460
Yeah.
没错。

1292
00:57:14.940 --> 00:57:16.340
And Andy goes, no.
安迪说，不是。

1293
00:57:16.640 --> 00:57:20.040
And he like wants to shout at Oscar so badly.
他当时特别想冲奥斯卡大吼。

1294
00:57:20.240 --> 00:57:22.220
And Ed is really funny in this scene.
艾德在这场戏里演得真好。

1295
00:57:22.360 --> 00:57:26.640
He goes, no, the kindness and gentle words of my anger management sponsor.
他说，不，是我的愤怒管理导师的善意和温言细语。

1296
00:57:26.640 --> 00:57:31.500
And his whole thing is, guys, my point is, maybe we can be that for Dwight.
他的核心意思是，伙计们，我的重点是，也许我们也能那样对待德怀特。

1297
00:57:31.720 --> 00:57:33.120
We can be that person.
我们可以成为那样的人。

1298
00:57:33.720 --> 00:57:34.080
Wow.
哇。

1299
00:57:35.600 --> 00:57:40.240
And Phyllis, coming in hard with the sass, says, look, we all do nice things.
菲利斯尖锐地反驳道，听着，我们都在做好事。

1300
00:57:40.400 --> 00:57:42.500
I bring in muffins at least once a week.
我每周至少带一次松饼来。

1301
00:57:42.860 --> 00:57:46.500
And Stanley says, those are leftover book group muffins.
斯坦利说，那些是读书会剩下的松饼。

1302
00:57:47.380 --> 00:57:48.500
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1303
00:57:48.500 --> 00:57:49.700
There's so much sass.
真是太刻薄了。

1304
00:57:50.200 --> 00:57:52.200
Anyway, Andy's like, hey, we're getting off topic.
总之，安迪说，嘿，我们跑题了。

1305
00:57:52.280 --> 00:57:53.220
He's coming back.
他要回来了。

1306
00:57:53.300 --> 00:57:54.860
Will you guys please give me some money?
你们能给我点钱吗？

1307
00:57:55.560 --> 00:58:00.660
So when Dwight gets the gift card and it pans to the bullpen, do you see how like everyone
所以当德怀特拿到礼品卡，镜头转到办公区时，你们看到大家

1308
00:58:00.660 --> 00:58:01.720
is like, whatever?
那种无所谓的态度了吗？

1309
00:58:02.140 --> 00:58:02.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1310
00:58:02.420 --> 00:58:03.660
That's why.
原因就在这儿。

1311
00:58:04.420 --> 00:58:05.000
Wow.
哇。

1312
00:58:05.800 --> 00:58:07.120
The shooting draft.
拍摄剧本。

1313
00:58:07.240 --> 00:58:08.240
The shooting draft.
拍摄剧本。

1314
00:58:08.700 --> 00:58:13.000
Well, Michael is going to ask Pam to come in his office.
迈克尔打算叫帕姆去他办公室。

1315
00:58:13.000 --> 00:58:13.900
It's about work.
是关于工作的。

1316
00:58:13.900 --> 00:58:14.800
It really is.
真的是。

1317
00:58:14.920 --> 00:58:16.360
It is about work.
确实是关于工作的。

1318
00:58:16.360 --> 00:58:17.180
It is.
没错。

1319
00:58:17.400 --> 00:58:17.800
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1320
00:58:18.320 --> 00:58:20.420
He is going to offer her a raise.
他打算给她加薪。

1321
00:58:21.120 --> 00:58:22.500
She's going to take it.
她会接受的。

1322
00:58:22.800 --> 00:58:23.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1323
00:58:23.620 --> 00:58:26.260
But it's still not changing her mood towards him.
但这依然改变不了她对他那种态度。

1324
00:58:26.260 --> 00:58:27.040
No.
没有。

1325
00:58:27.500 --> 00:58:33.220
And he wants her to know that the raise has strings attached from his heart to her mean
他想让她知道，这笔加薪是有附加条件的，源于他的一片真心，

1326
00:58:33.220 --> 00:58:33.700
attitude.
针对她恶劣的态度。

1327
00:58:36.160 --> 00:58:37.600
Pam's like, are you bribing me?
帕姆说，你是在贿赂我吗？

1328
00:58:37.700 --> 00:58:38.960
And then he's like, well, what do you want?
然后他说，那，你想要什么？

1329
00:58:39.060 --> 00:58:39.380
What do you want?
你想要什么？

1330
00:58:39.460 --> 00:58:40.420
Do you want a million dollars?
你想要一百万美元吗？

1331
00:58:40.580 --> 00:58:41.520
Do you want to hit me?
你想打我吗？

1332
00:58:42.120 --> 00:58:43.640
She says, I want to hit you.
她说，我想打你。

1333
00:58:44.440 --> 00:58:48.320
Lady, this plot line was so controversial.
天哪，这条剧情线当时争议太大了。

1334
00:58:49.240 --> 00:58:53.100
When this ended up airing, oh, my gosh, it lit up the message boards.
播出的时候，天哪，留言板都炸锅了。

1335
00:58:53.420 --> 00:58:53.980
I bet.
我敢肯定。

1336
00:58:53.980 --> 00:58:58.040
But not only does she want to hit him, but she says, in the parking lot in front of
但她不仅想打他，还说，在停车场当着

1337
00:58:58.040 --> 00:59:00.400
everyone, I'm going to hit you as hard as I can.
所有人的面，我要用尽全力打你。

1338
00:59:01.180 --> 00:59:03.300
Everyone gets very invested very quickly.
大家很快就都投入进去了。

1339
00:59:03.800 --> 00:59:06.020
There's a lot of chatter around the office.
办公室里议论纷纷。

1340
00:59:06.220 --> 00:59:10.020
And Toby is like, Pam, can I talk to you for a second?
托比说，帕姆，我能跟你谈谈吗？

1341
00:59:10.080 --> 00:59:13.080
We all think he's human resources and he's going to stop this.
我们都以为他是人力资源部的人，要来阻止这件事。

1342
00:59:13.380 --> 00:59:13.660
Yes.
没错。

1343
00:59:14.760 --> 00:59:18.460
But Toby just wants to confirm that she'll be hitting him off property.
但托比只是想确认她会不会在公司地界外打他。

1344
00:59:18.720 --> 00:59:21.360
And then he wants to show her how to throw a punch.
然后他还想教她怎么出拳。

1345
00:59:21.920 --> 00:59:22.960
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1346
00:59:23.660 --> 00:59:28.820
Charlie Grandy said that Paul is the one who pitched this bit.
查理·格兰迪说这个桥段是保罗提出来的。

1347
00:59:29.080 --> 00:59:31.780
He pitched it in the room during the rewrite.
他在重写剧本时的会议上提出来的。

1348
00:59:32.980 --> 00:59:36.400
And Charlie said he was pretty new on the office at this time.
查理说当时保罗刚进《办公室》剧组不久。

1349
00:59:36.620 --> 00:59:40.440
And when Paul was first pitching it, he thought, well, I don't know.
保罗刚提出来的时候，他心想，嗯，我不知道。

1350
00:59:40.520 --> 00:59:44.960
How are we going to – how is this going to, like, play realistically and funny?
这要怎么拍才能既真实又好笑呢？

1351
00:59:44.960 --> 00:59:47.360
But Paul was like, I know how to do it.
但保罗当时说，我知道该怎么做。

1352
00:59:47.480 --> 00:59:48.440
I know how to do it.
我知道该怎么做。

1353
00:59:49.180 --> 00:59:53.660
And he said that Paul just did it perfectly.
他说保罗做得非常完美。

1354
00:59:54.080 --> 00:59:54.380
Totally.
确实。

1355
00:59:54.380 --> 01:00:04.060
I also think this whole joke of Toby showing Pam how to throw a punch is a great example of a joke that lives in history in the character.
我也觉得托比教帕姆出拳这个笑话，很好地体现了角色背景故事中的历史感。

1356
01:00:04.060 --> 01:00:06.200
This is part of Toby's history.
这是托比个人历史的一部分。

1357
01:00:06.460 --> 01:00:06.800
Yes.
没错。

1358
01:00:06.880 --> 01:00:09.100
And we have gotten to know Toby so well.
我们已经非常了解托比了。

1359
01:00:09.280 --> 01:00:18.560
And we have seen years of Michael giving Toby, you know, such a hard time that, of course, of course, Toby's going to be like,
我们看了多年迈克尔给托比找麻烦，所以理所当然，托比会说，

1360
01:00:18.760 --> 01:00:21.980
so the power comes from your back foot when you want to turn.
所以当你想要转身时，力量来自你的后脚。

1361
01:00:21.980 --> 01:00:30.060
Because it's so clear, the joke is in the subtext, that Toby has fantasized about throwing a punch at Michael for years.
因为潜台词里的笑话很明显，托比多年来一直幻想能给迈克尔一拳。

1362
01:00:31.020 --> 01:00:40.880
We had a fan catch from Efrat T in Israel who just wanted to point out that when Michael hit Meredith with this car,
我们收到了一位来自以色列的粉丝Efrat T的发现，他想指出，当迈克尔开车撞到梅雷迪思时，

1363
01:00:41.140 --> 01:00:46.720
he tells Ryan that it was on company grounds because it was the parking lot.
他告诉瑞安那是在公司范围内，因为那是停车场。

1364
01:00:46.740 --> 01:00:47.940
Oh, good catch.
哦，好眼力。

1365
01:00:47.940 --> 01:00:56.040
But also in the duel, Andy and Dwight are fighting in the parking lot, and Jim tells them not to fight at work.
但在决斗那集里，安迪和德怀特在停车场打架，吉姆告诉他们不要在工作场所打架。

1366
01:00:56.760 --> 01:01:06.300
So just kind of pointing out, suddenly the parking lot is not company property, at least as far as Toby is concerned.
所以只是想指出，停车场突然就不算公司财产了，至少在托比看来是这样。

1367
01:01:07.140 --> 01:01:11.560
That is a really good catch because technically she'd have to try to throw a punch out in the street.
这确实是个很好的发现，因为严格来说，她得去街上试着出拳才行。

1368
01:01:11.840 --> 01:01:13.540
Or at least on the sidewalk.
或者至少得在人行道上。

1369
01:01:13.840 --> 01:01:14.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1370
01:01:14.840 --> 01:01:18.440
Well, speaking of the parking lot, everyone's gathered outside.
说到停车场，大家都聚集在外面。

1371
01:01:19.600 --> 01:01:21.100
Kevin's money is on Pam.
凯文赌帕姆赢。

1372
01:01:22.020 --> 01:01:24.960
Oscar notes it's a one-sided fight.
奥斯卡指出这是一场一边倒的战斗。

1373
01:01:25.240 --> 01:01:28.900
It's not really, you know, Pam winning is the only outcome here.
其实也不尽然，你知道，帕姆获胜是唯一的结果。

1374
01:01:29.580 --> 01:01:31.240
Well, right now there's no Michael.
嗯，现在迈克尔还没出现。

1375
01:01:31.440 --> 01:01:32.160
There's just Pam.
只有帕姆在。

1376
01:01:32.380 --> 01:01:33.600
We can't find Michael.
我们找不到迈克尔。

1377
01:01:33.780 --> 01:01:37.000
Meredith checks the men's room, says the toilet seat is still warm.
梅雷迪思检查了男厕所，说马桶圈还是热的。

1378
01:01:37.660 --> 01:01:40.740
Thanks for putting your hand on the toilet seat, Meredith.
谢谢你用手去摸马桶圈，梅雷迪思。

1379
01:01:41.020 --> 01:01:41.900
I guess so.
我想也是。

1380
01:01:42.160 --> 01:01:43.480
Kelly has made popcorn.
凯利做了爆米花。

1381
01:01:44.240 --> 01:01:45.760
Yes, she has.
没错，她做了。

1382
01:01:45.880 --> 01:01:47.040
She's bringing snacks.
她带了零食来。

1383
01:01:47.240 --> 01:01:49.180
And we find Michael in the stairwell.
然后我们在楼梯间找到了迈克尔。

1384
01:01:50.020 --> 01:01:50.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1385
01:01:51.000 --> 01:01:53.840
He's clearly trying to psych himself up for this moment.
他显然是在为这一刻给自己做心理建设。

1386
01:01:54.780 --> 01:01:56.980
And he walks out to the parking lot.
然后他走到了停车场。

1387
01:01:57.540 --> 01:01:59.560
And Pam is going to wind up.
帕姆准备挥拳了。

1388
01:01:59.760 --> 01:02:01.620
She's going to wind up for the punch.
她要蓄力出拳了。

1389
01:02:01.840 --> 01:02:02.740
He flinches.
他退缩了。

1390
01:02:03.360 --> 01:02:08.940
And can I just say that Angela Martin, for once, is on Pam's side.
我能说安吉拉·马丁这次难得地站在了帕姆这边吗。

1391
01:02:09.180 --> 01:02:10.300
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1392
01:02:10.440 --> 01:02:12.100
Your line is so funny.
你的台词太搞笑了。

1393
01:02:12.840 --> 01:02:15.680
Pam says, Michael, you have to put your hands down.
帕姆说，迈克尔，你得把手放下。

1394
01:02:15.860 --> 01:02:18.400
Angela says, put your hands in your pockets.
安吉拉说，把手插进兜里。

1395
01:02:18.400 --> 01:02:24.420
So this is just another person who is excited for Michael to get hit.
所以这又是一个期待迈克尔挨揍的人。

1396
01:02:24.420 --> 01:02:28.680
Well, as Pam is getting ready to hit Michael, he actually stops.
好吧，就在帕姆准备打迈克尔时，他竟然停下了。

1397
01:02:28.840 --> 01:02:31.620
He apologizes to her for everything.
他为之前的一切向她道歉。

1398
01:02:32.400 --> 01:02:33.760
Pam takes it in.
帕姆接受了道歉。

1399
01:02:33.800 --> 01:02:34.800
And she's like, OK.
她说，好吧。

1400
01:02:35.440 --> 01:02:35.840
OK.
好吧。

1401
01:02:36.000 --> 01:02:37.180
She says, fine.
她说，好吧。

1402
01:02:37.320 --> 01:02:39.760
Don't date anyone else in my family ever again.
以后别再跟我家里任何人约会了。

1403
01:02:39.780 --> 01:02:41.560
And she's going to walk away.
然后她转身就要走。

1404
01:02:41.760 --> 01:02:42.480
She is.
确实如此。

1405
01:02:42.700 --> 01:02:45.740
But Michael cannot shut his mouth.
但迈克尔就是管不住自己的嘴。

1406
01:02:46.140 --> 01:02:46.640
Yeah.
没错。

1407
01:02:46.640 --> 01:02:50.880
He says, for the record, your mom came on to me.
他说，郑重声明，是你妈先勾引我的。

1408
01:02:53.660 --> 01:03:00.840
Pam pivots on her heel and slaps him so hard across the face.
帕姆脚下一转，狠狠地给了他一记耳光。

1409
01:03:00.980 --> 01:03:06.100
And she's got that superhuman pregnancy strength per Kelly.
据凯莉说，她当时拥有孕妇超人的力量。

1410
01:03:06.440 --> 01:03:07.500
We got a lot of mail.
我们收到了很多邮件。

1411
01:03:07.680 --> 01:03:09.820
I might say fan mail flurry.
我甚至可以说是一阵粉丝来信的旋风。

1412
01:03:10.300 --> 01:03:10.620
Oh.
噢。

1413
01:03:10.960 --> 01:03:11.700
Enoch N.
来自宾夕法尼亚州的伊诺克·N.

1414
01:03:11.820 --> 01:03:15.060
from Pennsylvania wants to know, did Jenna really slap Steve?
想知道，珍娜真的打了史蒂夫吗？

1415
01:03:15.060 --> 01:03:17.900
And Angela, Katie M.
还有安吉拉，来自加州弗雷斯诺的凯蒂·M.

1416
01:03:18.040 --> 01:03:20.560
from Fresno, California said, quote,
写道，引用如下：

1417
01:03:21.460 --> 01:03:28.280
the moment Pam slaps Michael, I absolutely believe Jenna could have played Sidney Bristow on Alias.
帕姆打迈克尔的那一刻，我绝对相信珍娜能演《双面女间谍》里的悉尼·布里斯托。

1418
01:03:28.340 --> 01:03:29.220
Oh, Katie.
噢，凯蒂。

1419
01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:31.340
OK, fine, Katie.
好吧，凯蒂。

1420
01:03:31.620 --> 01:03:32.140
I agree.
我同意。

1421
01:03:32.320 --> 01:03:35.100
This is a real Pam kicking some butt moment.
这真是帕姆大显身手的时刻。

1422
01:03:35.700 --> 01:03:36.740
Jenna, you nailed it.
珍娜，你演得太棒了。

1423
01:03:36.940 --> 01:03:42.520
I am also curious because my character, as you know, slaps two people on this show.
我也很好奇，因为如你所知，我的角色在这部剧中打过两个人。

1424
01:03:42.520 --> 01:03:45.580
And I really did hit my co-stars.
而且我确实打到了我的搭档。

1425
01:03:45.900 --> 01:03:48.380
Did you really hit Steve?
你真的打了史蒂夫吗？

1426
01:03:48.920 --> 01:03:50.000
I did not.
我没有。

1427
01:03:50.620 --> 01:03:53.020
Steve said I should hit him.
史蒂夫说我应该打他。

1428
01:03:53.480 --> 01:03:57.600
It did not seem safe to me because I am whipping around.
我觉得那样做不安全，因为我当时是在转身。

1429
01:03:57.700 --> 01:04:05.700
If it was just a slap from a standing position, but this was like, I could not bring myself to do it.
如果只是站着打一巴掌还行，但当时的情况是，我实在下不去手。

1430
01:04:05.700 --> 01:04:10.500
I think that's really smart because I hit Mike Schur on the run.
我觉得你很聪明，因为我是在奔跑中打了迈克·舒尔。

1431
01:04:10.500 --> 01:04:12.360
Your whole body goes into it.
你全身的力气都用上了。

1432
01:04:12.620 --> 01:04:15.620
And he discussed that slap on our podcaSt.
他在我们的播客里讨论过那一巴掌。

1433
01:04:16.420 --> 01:04:19.220
Well, our stunt coordinator, Eric Solke.
嗯，我们的特技协调员埃里克·索尔克。

1434
01:04:19.820 --> 01:04:20.800
Love, Eric.
爱死埃里克了。

1435
01:04:21.160 --> 01:04:21.640
Yes.
没错。

1436
01:04:21.640 --> 01:04:26.520
He gave me very detailed instructions on how to pretend slap Steve.
他给了我非常详细的指导，教我如何假装打史蒂夫。

1437
01:04:27.260 --> 01:04:35.300
And he also worked with Matt Sohn on positioning the camera behind me so that you couldn't even tell that I'm not hitting him.
他还和马特·索恩一起配合，把摄像机放在我身后，这样你就根本看不出我没打到他。

1438
01:04:35.780 --> 01:04:40.640
And then Randy told me that we added that slap sound in post-production.
后来兰迪告诉我，那个耳光声是后期制作加进去的。

1439
01:04:41.280 --> 01:04:44.080
So I did not slap Steve.
所以我并没有打史蒂夫。

1440
01:04:44.860 --> 01:04:47.600
Well, I'm glad you didn't because also you couldn't see him.
嗯，我很高兴你没打，因为当时你也看不见他。

1441
01:04:47.820 --> 01:04:49.280
Your back was to him.
你背对着他。

1442
01:04:49.380 --> 01:04:49.720
Yes.
是的。

1443
01:04:49.720 --> 01:04:51.940
That's what I was worried about.
我担心的就是这个。

1444
01:04:52.440 --> 01:04:56.860
I mean, I was worried that I might make contact, but I was very specific.
我是说，我担心可能会碰到他，所以我非常谨慎。

1445
01:04:57.060 --> 01:04:58.460
Like, we lined up our bodies.
比如，我们对齐了身体位置。

1446
01:04:59.040 --> 01:05:01.940
My pivot was highly choreographed.
我的转身动作是经过精心编排的。

1447
01:05:02.040 --> 01:05:04.340
I just pivoted on that one spot.
我就在那一个点上转身。

1448
01:05:04.800 --> 01:05:05.060
Yeah.
没错。

1449
01:05:05.340 --> 01:05:06.380
You guys sold it.
你们演得太逼真了。

1450
01:05:06.520 --> 01:05:08.200
I thought it totally worked.
我觉得效果非常好。

1451
01:05:08.500 --> 01:05:11.920
Well, at the end, Michael is limping away.
最后，迈克尔一瘸一拐地走开了。

1452
01:05:12.660 --> 01:05:13.160
Limping?
一瘸一拐？

1453
01:05:13.480 --> 01:05:13.960
I know.
我知道。

1454
01:05:14.100 --> 01:05:15.280
And Dwight's like, why are you limping?
德怀特问他，你为什么一瘸一拐的？

1455
01:05:15.380 --> 01:05:16.460
He's like, I don't know.
他说，我不知道。

1456
01:05:16.460 --> 01:05:19.400
So, well, we had a fan question from M.E.L.
我们收到了一位来自马里兰州巴尔的摩的粉丝M.E.L.的提问。

1457
01:05:19.400 --> 01:05:20.680
in Baltimore, Maryland.
来自马里兰州巴尔的摩。

1458
01:05:21.420 --> 01:05:25.620
Was Michael's limping and Dwight's reaction scripted or improvised?
迈克尔一瘸一拐的样子和德怀特的反应是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的？

1459
01:05:26.080 --> 01:05:27.240
It was scripted.
是剧本写的。

1460
01:05:27.780 --> 01:05:27.980
Yeah.
没错。

1461
01:05:28.100 --> 01:05:33.660
When I reread the shooting draft, almost every single thing you see was completely scripted.
当我重读拍摄剧本时，几乎你看到的每一件事都是完全写好的。

1462
01:05:33.800 --> 01:05:35.040
All the little details.
所有那些小细节。

1463
01:05:35.300 --> 01:05:35.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1464
01:05:36.060 --> 01:05:39.120
Well, fans had very mixed reactions to this slap.
粉丝们对这一巴掌的反应非常不一。

1465
01:05:39.900 --> 01:05:40.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1466
01:05:40.480 --> 01:05:43.600
A lot of people felt like it was one step too far.
很多人觉得这有点太过分了。

1467
01:05:43.780 --> 01:05:46.040
They did not like Pam for doing this.
他们不喜欢帕姆这样做。

1468
01:05:46.460 --> 01:05:51.880
I think Steve is so good at playing the vulnerable side of Michael.
我觉得史蒂夫非常擅长演绎迈克尔脆弱的一面。

1469
01:05:52.700 --> 01:05:53.820
People were upset.
大家都很生气。

1470
01:05:54.220 --> 01:05:56.860
How did we feel about it and re-watching it?
我们当时是怎么想的，现在重看又是什么感觉？

1471
01:05:57.720 --> 01:06:02.220
I mean, I thought, you know, Pam was walking away.
我是说，我觉得，你知道，帕姆当时正要走开。

1472
01:06:02.940 --> 01:06:04.460
She wasn't going to do it.
她本来不打算动手的。

1473
01:06:04.720 --> 01:06:05.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1474
01:06:05.160 --> 01:06:08.580
And Michael just couldn't leave it alone.
但迈克尔就是不肯罢休。

1475
01:06:09.180 --> 01:06:28.280
I think that collectively, I remember the writers and producers felt that we couldn't end this story of Michael dating Pam's mom, doing this, like, highly insensitive thing to Pam.
我想大家一致认为，编剧和制片人都觉得，我们不能让迈克尔和帕姆妈妈约会这件事，以这种对帕姆极其不敏感的方式结束。

1476
01:06:28.280 --> 01:06:35.620
Not only did he date her mom, he then broke up with her mom on her birthday in a public place.
他不仅和她妈妈约会，还在她妈妈生日那天在公共场合和她分手。

1477
01:06:36.520 --> 01:06:39.100
And he needed a comeuppance, basically.
基本上，他需要受到惩罚。

1478
01:06:39.100 --> 01:06:40.740
He needed, yes, he did.
他确实需要，没错。

1479
01:06:40.960 --> 01:06:43.100
Him and Pam needed to settle this.
他和帕姆需要解决这件事。

1480
01:06:43.220 --> 01:06:44.380
And now it's settled.
现在解决了。

1481
01:06:44.680 --> 01:06:46.640
It's not going to fester.
这不会再发酵了。

1482
01:06:47.300 --> 01:06:55.720
So, that was, I think, the reasoning behind it was that we needed to, this was now, it's been resolved.
所以，我想这就是背后的逻辑，我们需要让这件事得到解决。

1483
01:06:56.460 --> 01:07:02.980
You know, there were a few relationships on the show that reminded me of siblings, like Angela, Oscar, and Kevin.
你知道，剧里有几段关系让我想起兄妹，比如安吉拉、奥斯卡和凯文。

1484
01:07:03.280 --> 01:07:05.140
They were almost like siblings, you know?
他们就像兄妹一样，你懂吗？

1485
01:07:05.360 --> 01:07:06.460
Stanley and Phyllis.
斯坦利和菲利斯。

1486
01:07:06.560 --> 01:07:07.640
Stanley and Phyllis.
斯坦利和菲利斯。

1487
01:07:07.640 --> 01:07:11.040
And I felt like Pam and Michael were like brother and sister.
我觉得帕姆和迈克尔就像兄妹一样。

1488
01:07:11.320 --> 01:07:13.100
I think that's a really good analogy.
我觉得这个比喻非常贴切。

1489
01:07:13.940 --> 01:07:17.420
But, yeah, I remember people were really chatting about this.
不过，我记得当时大家确实在热议这件事。

1490
01:07:18.320 --> 01:07:23.600
Dwight is going to bring Michael inside, and he says he's got some chicken he can put on that.
德怀特要把迈克尔带进去，他说他有鸡肉可以敷在上面。

1491
01:07:23.720 --> 01:07:25.700
Call back to all that chicken on the microwave.
呼应了微波炉里那些鸡肉的梗。

1492
01:07:26.420 --> 01:07:28.120
Fan question from Victoria H.
来自俄亥俄州哥伦布市的维多利亚·H的粉丝提问。

1493
01:07:28.220 --> 01:07:29.180
in Columbus, Ohio.
来自俄亥俄州哥伦布市。

1494
01:07:29.540 --> 01:07:34.460
Was Dwight holding real raw chicken on Michael's face, or did Phil Shea make that?
德怀特敷在迈克尔脸上的鸡肉是真的吗，还是道具师菲尔·谢做的？

1495
01:07:35.020 --> 01:07:36.100
Well, both.
嗯，两者都有。

1496
01:07:36.100 --> 01:07:41.280
It is real chicken that Phil Shea, like, shrink-wrapped.
那是真的鸡肉，菲尔·谢把它用保鲜膜包起来了。

1497
01:07:42.600 --> 01:07:47.200
So, it was real, but it was, like, covered in something so that.
所以它是真的，但它被什么东西覆盖着，所以……

1498
01:07:48.220 --> 01:07:48.700
Gross.
恶心。

1499
01:07:49.720 --> 01:07:51.060
That is so gross.
太恶心了。

1500
01:07:51.060 --> 01:07:54.420
I thought for sure you're going to say, no, it's a fakie rubber chicken thing.
我本来以为你肯定会说，不，那是假的橡胶鸡道具。

1501
01:07:54.680 --> 01:07:56.520
No, it was real chicken.
不，那是真的鸡肉。

1502
01:07:56.980 --> 01:07:57.460
Wowzers.
哇哦。

1503
01:07:57.860 --> 01:07:58.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1504
01:07:58.960 --> 01:08:02.440
Well, Dwight thinks he finally did his favor, and he says, fire, Jim.
嗯，德怀特觉得他终于帮上忙了，他说，开火吧，吉姆。

1505
01:08:03.020 --> 01:08:04.020
Michael's like, no.
迈克尔说，不行。

1506
01:08:04.020 --> 01:08:06.740
So, Dwight is angry and takes his dinner away.
所以，德怀特很生气，把他的晚餐拿走了。

1507
01:08:07.480 --> 01:08:07.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1508
01:08:08.640 --> 01:08:11.560
He's going to eat that after it was on Michael's face.
他竟然要在迈克尔脸上蹭过之后吃掉它。

1509
01:08:11.980 --> 01:08:12.420
Apparently.
显然是这样。

1510
01:08:13.000 --> 01:08:17.420
You know, I feel like this episode wraps up best with the talking head that Michael had.
你知道，我觉得这一集最好用迈克尔的那个采访片段来收尾。

1511
01:08:17.960 --> 01:08:18.400
Yes.
没错。

1512
01:08:18.500 --> 01:08:19.640
I feel like I need to read it.
我觉得我得读一下。

1513
01:08:19.760 --> 01:08:20.520
Okay, please do.
好的，请读吧。

1514
01:08:20.520 --> 01:08:27.220
As I watched Pam's big, strong hand coming towards my face, I saw my entire life flash
当我看着帕姆那只又大又有力的手向我的脸挥过来时，我看到我的一生在

1515
01:08:27.220 --> 01:08:28.140
before my eyes.
眼前闪过。

1516
01:08:28.260 --> 01:08:29.000
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1517
01:08:29.200 --> 01:08:33.820
I have four kids, and I have a hover car, and a hover house.
我有四个孩子，还有一辆悬浮车，和一栋悬浮房子。

1518
01:08:34.020 --> 01:08:36.860
And my wife is a runner, and it shows.
我的妻子是个跑步健将，身材很好。

1519
01:08:37.220 --> 01:08:41.320
And Pam and Jim are my best friends, and our kids play together.
帕姆和吉姆是我最好的朋友，我们的孩子一起玩耍。

1520
01:08:41.320 --> 01:08:45.980
And I am happy, and I am rich, and I never die.
我很快乐，我很富有，而且我永远不会死。

1521
01:08:46.340 --> 01:08:49.480
It doesn't sound like much, but it's enough for me.
听起来没什么大不了的，但对我来说这就足够了。

1522
01:08:50.140 --> 01:08:51.340
There you have it.
就是这样。

1523
01:08:51.460 --> 01:08:52.400
There you have it.
就是这样。

1524
01:08:53.220 --> 01:08:57.720
Michael, in the end, just sees them as his family.
迈克尔最终还是把他们看作自己的家人。

1525
01:08:58.360 --> 01:08:58.980
Always.
一直都是。

1526
01:08:59.320 --> 01:08:59.660
Always.
一直都是。

1527
01:09:00.780 --> 01:09:04.320
Next week, you guys, buckle in, because it is murder.
下周，各位，系好安全带，因为我们要讲“谋杀”那一集了。

1528
01:09:04.920 --> 01:09:05.480
Ugh.
呃。

1529
